  "comments": {
    "@bdqjtggr1grfn66h946dhjh0ft": "a + b: the one + works part by part on points, directions, colours, or any record whose fields are all Float64s; plus is its old name, kept for a release. This module's operations and their names follow the built-in functions of GLSL and WGSL (influence), which a shader compiles them to.",
    "@0l0fl1nj40vcvh8bp2u5sb51cr": "a − b: the old name of −, kept for a release. The direction from b to a.",
    "@dfqk15d2jbh7gn0g057ofmf4tn": "a · b: the old name of ·, kept for a release. A colour tinted by another.",
    "@gpr2icg8543tmnss26ricahd08": "Every part of v times by: a direction made longer, a colour made brighter.",
    "@bsh2hsvcrpov7nqglt3ehur72p": "The parts' products added up: how much a and b point the same way.",
    "@398l7be8o1ao8vljcpllcum7qf": "How long v is: √(v · v).",
    "@8krpouj1med1u8g6r19150u502": "How far a is from b.",
    "@k9fr8o3154secpp3c3hegd2okf": "v scaled to length 1 (normalize on a GPU).",
    "@vshgss85bifvhke0t02estkjid": "a when amount is 0, b when it is 1, and in between, part by part.",
    "@m391m4mr8rc457pi2icf8foqik": "Every part of v kept between low and high.",
    "@t00b0t42fe9h0rreh10m9k0s9p": "A ray going this direction, bounced off a surface facing normal (normal of length 1)."
  },
